  "raw_text": "240\n\nDakwi takaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto separate, to become separated\n \n(either marital, or from a friend, or from a church or other\norganization) / separarse, separarse (ya sea conyugal, o de un amigo, o de una iglesia u otra organización)\n\nDakwi takaia lâka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nseparation\n \n(either marital, or from a friend, or from a church or other\norganization) / separación (ya sea marital, o de un amigo, o de una iglesia u otra organización)\n\nSilp dakwi takaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto disassociate oneself\n \n/ disociarse\n\nDanh takaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto come to be finished, to come to completion\n \n/ llegar a ser terminado, llegar a su finalización.\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nmwb-08/19\n):\n \nSiknis nani sut ba yu kum dahn takbia ki?\n \n–\n \nWill there come to be a day when all sicknesses are done?\n\n/ ¿Llegará el día en que todas las enfermedades terminen?)\n\nDanh\n \nâ\npu takaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto\n \ncease to exist\n \n/ dejar de existir\n\n(\nEx/Ej\n(\nbh58\n):\n \nUpla kum pruya taim, dan\n \nâ\npu takisa\n \n–\n \nWhen a person dies, (they) cease to exist\n \n/ Cuando una\n\npersona muere, (ellos) dejan de existir\n)\n\nDanh\n \ntakaia bîla\n \nnani ba\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nconcluding words, words to\n \nfinish\n \n/ palabras finales, palabras para\n\nterminar\n\nDibors takaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto become divorced\n \n/ divorciarse\n\nDibors takaia lâka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \ndivorce\n \n/ divorcio\n\nDutki takaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto become strong, to become firm, to become tight\n \n/ volverse fuerte, hacerse firme, apretarse\n\nIrbi takaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto cut off, to chop off\n \n/ cortar\n\nKakaira takaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto get to know, to get acquainted, to come to know\n \n/ llegar a conocer, venir a conocer\n\n(Ex/Ej(\ndb-1 Timoti 2:4\n):\n \nkasak tanka ba sin witin nani kakaira taki banhbia\n \n–\n \nalso their coming to know the truth\n \n/ también\nhan llegado a conocer la verdad)\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nmwb-06/20\n):\n \nMoses ba Jehova ra kau kakaira takaia want kan bara witin nina tânka ba sin\n \n–\n \nMoses was wanting to\ncome to know Jehovah better and also to come to know the understanding of his name\n \n/ Moisés quería conocer mejor a\nJehová y también conocer el significado de su nombre)\n\nKli kupia kumi takaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto restore peace\n \n/ restaurar la paz\n\nKupia kumi takaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto make peace happen, to make peace, to come to be of one heart\n \n/ hacer que la paz\n\nsuceda, hacer las paces, llegar a ser de un solo\n \ncorazón\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nlfb\n-\nsection3\n-\nintro\n):\n \nisti kupia kumi takaia\n \n–\n \nto make peace happen quickly\n \n/ hacer las paces rápidamente\n)\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nwqu\n-\n03/30\n):\n \nMatiu 5:23,24 aisi ba baku, dîa muni kupia kumi takaia sa ki yawan mapara saura luki kristian uplika\n\nkum wal?\n \n–\n \nAs it says at Matthew 5:23,24, why are we to (must we) make peace happen with a Christian who has bad\n\nthinking with regards to (something against) us?\n \n/ Como se dice en Mateo 5:23,24, ¿por qué debemos hacer que la paz\n\nsuceda con un cristiano que\n \ntiene malos pensamientos con respecto a (algo en contra) de nosotros?\n)\n\nKli kupia kumi takaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto restore peace\n \n/ restaurar la paz\n\nKupia kumi takaia\n \nl\nâ\nka\n \n(\nn/s\n)\n \n–\n \nre\nconciliation\n \n/ re\nconciliaci\nó\nn\n\nKwihra takaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto become pregnant\n \n/ quedar embarazada\n\n(\nEx/Ej\n(\nlfb69\n):\n \nKwihra takma bara luhpa waitna kum baikma\n \n–\n \nYou will become pregnant and you will give birth to a male\n\nchild\n \n/ Quedarás embarazada y tendr\ná\n \nun hijo\n)\n\nLamni takaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto become calm\n \n/ calmarse\n\nLamni taks!\n \n(v-imp)\n \n–\n \nBe calm!, Be still!\n \n/ Estate tranquilo!, Estate quieto!\n\nLan takaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto learn, to get training\n \n/ aprender, entrenar\n\n(Ex/Ej:\n \nLan takan\n \n–\n \nwe learned\n \n(inclusive yawan form),\n \nhe/she learned\n \n(v-3p-past) / aprendimos (forma inclusiva de yawan),\nél/ella aprendió (v-3p-pasado))\n\nLan takaia brinka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \ndesire to learn, desire to be trained\n \n/ deseo de aprender, deseo de ser\nentrenado\n\nLan takan daukaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto desire to learn\n \n/ desear aprender\n\nLan takan ai daukisa\n \n–\n \nI desire to learn\n \n/ Deseo aprender\n\nLan takan mai daukisa\n \n–\n \nYou desire to learn\n \n/ Deseas aprender\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nlff-1\n):\n \nBaibil wina dîa lan takan mai daukisa?\n \n–\n \nWhat do you desire to learn from the Bible?\n \n/ ¿Qué\ndeseas aprender de la Biblia?)\n\nLapta takaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto grow hot\n \n(often referring to the day becoming hotter) / calentarse (a menudo refiriéndose a\nque el día se calienta más)\n\nLaptika takaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto sweat, to perspire\n \n/ sudar, transpirar\n\nLatan takaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto become clear, to become visible, to become apparent\n \n/ hacerse claro, hacerse visible,\nhacerse evidente",
